;; numerics.corpus -- numerics gap corpus (pending). Every form on this
;; list currently DIVERGES between real Clojure 1.13.0-alpha6 and mova;
;; it is a ledger of failures, not aspirational syntax. Covers: integer
;; overflow + the `'`-suffixed promoting family + `unchecked-*`
;; wraparound, ratios, BigInt/BigDecimal contagion,
;; clojure.math + java.lang.Math interop, NaN?/infinite?, float printing
;; exactness (##Inf/##NaN/scientific notation), numeric casts (byte/
;; short/num), and parse-boolean/parse-uuid/rand existence. quot/rem/mod
;; sign-matrix and *basic* bit-and/or/xor/not/shift-left/shift-right,
;; int/long/double/float casts, and -0.0 printing all already CONFORM --
;; see tests/conformance/corpus/numbers.corpus (bottom) instead; they are
;; deliberately not repeated here.
;;
;; S5 (SPEC-numtower) paid off most of this file: 27 of its original 44
;; forms were promoted into tests/conformance/corpus/numbers.corpus once
;; mova got real tower arithmetic (the `'`-suffixed promoting family, the
;; `unchecked-*` family, ratios, BigInt/BigDecimal contagion, `==`,
;; `rationalize`, `ratio?`/`rational?`/`decimal?`, `NaN?`/`infinite?`).
;; `(= 1 1.0)` was a documented deviation when this file was written and
;; is one no longer -- `=` is numeric-category-strict now and the
;; DEVIATIONS.md row is gone. What is LEFT below is the genuinely
;; unfinished numerics: the bit-op family mova lacks
;; (unsigned-bit-shift-right/bit-test/bit-set/bit-flip/bit-clear),
;; clojure.math + java.lang.Math interop gaps, parse-boolean/parse-uuid,
;; and the subnormal/float-printing digit divergences.
;;
;;PRELUDE (require (quote [clojure.math]))
(inc 9223372036854775807)
(dec -9223372036854775808)
(* 3037000500 3037000500)
(+ 9223372036854775807 1)
(- -9223372036854775808 1)
(byte 130)
(short 40000)
;; Denormal float printing: Rust's shortest-round-trip digits for
;; Double.MIN_VALUE are "5e-324" where Java's FloatingDecimal prints
;; "4.9E-324" -- same bit pattern, different text (S12's re-layout printer
;; assumes digit parity, which holds everywhere EXCEPT subnormals).
4.9E-324
;; S3: the SAME divergence, reached via the Double/MIN_VALUE static field
;; itself (src/builtins/statics.rs) rather than a bare literal -- the
;; registered value is bit-for-bit correct (numerics-comparison forms
;; using it conform, see tests/conformance/corpus/interop-statics.corpus),
;; only the bare pr-str of it diverges, same as the literal above.
Double/MIN_VALUE
;; S3: Float/MAX_VALUE (src/builtins/statics.rs) -- mova has no real f32,
;; so it stores f32::MAX WIDENED to f64 (numerically exact: 3.4028234663852886E38),
;; but prints that with full f64 shortest-round-trip precision where
;; Java's Float.toString prints its own shorter f32-precision digits
;; ("3.4028235E38") -- same "numerically right, printed wrong" shape as
;; Double/MIN_VALUE above, not a subnormal but the analogous single-vs-
;; double-precision printer gap.
Float/MAX_VALUE
